---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const schema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@graph': [
  { '@type': 'Article', 'headline': 'Why Meta Ads ROAS and GA4 Ecommerce Revenue Do Not Match', 'description': 'A practical reconciliation framework for differences between Meta Ads reporting and GA4 ecommerce revenue.', 'url': 'https://visible-ads.com/meta-ads-ga4-revenue-mismatch', 'datePublished': '2026-09-13', 'dateModified': '2026-09-13', 'author': { '@type': 'Organization', 'name': 'Visible Ads', 'url': 'https://visible-ads.com' }, 'publisher': { '@type': 'Organization', 'name': 'Visible Ads', 'url': 'https://visible-ads.com' } },
  { '@type': 'FAQPage', 'mainEntity': [{ '@type': 'Question', 'name': 'Why is Meta ROAS different from GA4 ecommerce revenue?', 'acceptedAnswer': { '@type': 'Answer', 'text': 'Meta Ads and GA4 can apply different attribution models, conversion definitions, time zones, reporting dates and levels of observed or modelled data. A difference does not prove either system is wrong.' } }, { '@type': 'Question', 'name': 'Which number should an ecommerce business trust?', 'acceptedAnswer': { '@type': 'Answer', 'text': 'Use validated order and finance data to judge realised revenue and contribution. Use platform and analytics reports to understand channel signals after aligning their definitions and time periods.' } }, { '@type': 'Question', 'name': 'Can GA4 and Meta be reconciled exactly?', 'acceptedAnswer': { '@type': 'Answer', 'text': 'They can be made more comparable, but they will not always match exactly. Reconcile at order level where possible and document the attribution and revenue rules used in each view.' } }] },
  { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', 'itemListElement': [{ '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 1, 'name': 'Home', 'item': 'https://visible-ads.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 2, 'name': 'Meta Ads and GA4 Revenue Mismatch', 'item': 'https://visible-ads.com/meta-ads-ga4-revenue-mismatch' }] }
] };
---
<Layout title="Why Meta Ads ROAS and GA4 Revenue Do Not Match | Visible Ads" description="Diagnose the difference between Meta Ads ROAS and GA4 ecommerce revenue with an order-level reconciliation framework." schema={schema}>
  <section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-navy-light relative overflow-hidden" data-animate><div class="absolute inset-0 dot-pattern opacity-5"></div><div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative"><nav class="text-sm text-slate-light mb-8"><a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span class="text-white">Meta Ads and GA4 revenue</span></nav><div class="max-w-3xl"><span class="inline-block px-4 py-1.5 bg-electric/20 text-electric-light text-sm font-medium rounded-full mb-6">Measurement diagnosis</span><h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-heading font-extrabold text-white leading-tight mb-6">Why Meta Ads ROAS and GA4 Ecommerce Revenue Do Not Match</h1><p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-light leading-relaxed">Meta and GA4 usually answer different attribution questions. Reconcile the definitions and the orders first, then use each report for the decision it can support.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>The short answer</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Meta Ads can credit a conversion according to the account's attribution setting, while GA4 applies its own reporting and channel rules. The two tools can also use different event definitions, dates, time zones and levels of observed or modelled data.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A revenue mismatch is a diagnostic signal, not proof that one platform is lying. The commercial decision should rest on validated orders, refunds and contribution economics.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">What each system is measuring</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><caption class="sr-only">Comparison of Meta Ads, GA4 and order data</caption><thead class="bg-navy text-white"><tr><th class="p-4">View</th><th class="p-4">Best use</th><th class="p-4">Check before comparing</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-700"><tr class="border-t"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Meta Ads</th><td class="p-4">Platform attribution and optimisation signals.</td><td class="p-4">Attribution setting, event, reporting date, time zone and revenue value.</td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">GA4</th><td class="p-4">Site and channel analysis under GA4's reporting rules.</td><td class="p-4">Key event, attribution model, channel grouping, consent and event versus interaction time.</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Orders and finance data</th><td class="p-4">Realised revenue, refunds, discounts and contribution decisions.</td><td class="p-4">Order status, tax and shipping treatment, refund date and product cost.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>Common causes of the gap</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Attribution differences are the usual cause. GA4 uses data-driven attribution by default for event-scoped reporting, while session and user traffic-source views use paid-and-organic last click. Meta reporting follows the account's configured attribution rules.</p><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><li><strong>Different credit rules:</strong> a platform can assign credit to an interaction that a last-click channel report does not show.</li><li><strong>Different clocks:</strong> interaction date and purchase date can place the same order in different reporting periods.</li><li><strong>Different conversion definitions:</strong> purchase events, duplicate handling, discounts, tax, shipping and refunds may not be treated alike.</li><li><strong>Incomplete observation:</strong> consent choices, browser restrictions, cross-device journeys and technical failures can change what analytics sees.</li><li><strong>Feed or tracking faults:</strong> incorrect values, duplicate purchase events, missing identifiers or broken campaign parameters can create a genuine implementation problem.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>How to reconcile Meta and GA4</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Start with one defined comparison. Use the same market, currency, time zone, order status and revenue treatment before looking at channel credit.</p><ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><li>Export paid orders for the comparison period and remove test, cancelled or duplicate orders under a documented rule.</li><li>Confirm that the Meta purchase value and the GA4 purchase value use the same currency, tax, shipping and discount treatment.</li><li>Record the Meta attribution setting and the GA4 report, dimension and attribution model used.</li><li>Compare event time with ad-interaction time rather than mixing them without a note.</li><li>Sample individual orders and journeys for duplicates, missing events, unwanted referral sources and broken campaign parameters.</li><li>Judge scale using <a href="/roas-vs-profit" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">revenue ROAS and contribution</a>, not a reconciled dashboard total alone.</li></ol></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>When a mismatch needs a tracking fix</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">A stable, explained difference can be normal. An abrupt change, a duplicated purchase pattern, missing order values or a mismatch that prevents commercial decisions needs investigation.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A measurement audit checks the event path before budget changes. It then connects the finding to the <a href="/paid-social" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">Meta Ads account</a>, the <a href="/how-we-audit" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">audit process</a> and the order data that finance can validate.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>Primary measurement references</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Use product documentation to verify the settings in the specific account. Do not assume an attribution model or reporting view from an old implementation.</p><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><li><a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/10596865" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">Google Analytics: key event attribution models report</a></li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11080067" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">Google Analytics: scopes of traffic-source dimensions</a></li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/10710245" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">Google Analytics: modelled key events</a></li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="relative py-20 lg:py-28 bg-navy" data-animate><div class="absolute inset-0 dot-pattern opacity-5"></div><div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center"><h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-white mb-6">Need a defensible revenue view?</h2><p class="text-lg text-slate-light mb-8">We can audit the tracking, attribution settings and commercial definitions before you change spend.</p><a href="/free-ads-audit" class="w-full sm:w-auto inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-cta text-white font-semibold px-10 py-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-electric transition-colors text-lg">Request an ads audit</a></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="space-y-4"><details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-heading font-semibold text-navy">Why is Meta ROAS different from GA4 ecommerce revenue?</summary><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Meta Ads and GA4 can apply different attribution models, conversion definitions, time zones, reporting dates and levels of observed or modelled data. A difference does not prove either system is wrong.</p></details><details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-heading font-semibold text-navy">Which number should an ecommerce business trust?</summary><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Use validated order and finance data to judge realised revenue and contribution. Use platform and analytics reports to understand channel signals after aligning their definitions and time periods.</p></details><details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-heading font-semibold text-navy">Can GA4 and Meta be reconciled exactly?</summary><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">They can be made more comparable, but they will not always match exactly. Reconcile at order level where possible and document the attribution and revenue rules used in each view.</p></details></div></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">Compare like with like</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">ROAS is a ratio. Revenue is a currency amount. Compare Meta purchase conversion value with GA4 Meta-attributed purchase revenue, or divide both revenue figures by the same Meta spend. Do not compare a 4.0 ROAS ratio with GBP 20,000 of revenue.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">For a documented comparison, state the GA4 report and dimension used, such as a session traffic-source view or an event-scoped attribution report. Attribution differences can cause a gap, so record the Meta ad-set attribution setting before treating the difference as a tracking fault.</p></div></section>
</Layout>
